# Configuration System

## Purpose
Defines how to access and use configuration values in SND macros.

## Scope
This rule covers configuration access patterns, type conversion, and usage examples.

## Configuration Access Pattern

### Basic Access
```lua
-- Always use Config.Get() to access configuration values
local settingValue = Config.Get("SettingName")

-- Convert to appropriate type when needed
local numericValue = tonumber(Config.Get("NumericSetting"))
local booleanValue = Config.Get("BooleanSetting") == "true"
```

### Type-Safe Access Functions
```lua
-- Get configuration with type conversion
function GetConfigAsString(key, defaultValue)
    return Config.Get(key) or defaultValue or ""
end

function GetConfigAsNumber(key, defaultValue)
    local value = Config.Get(key)
    return value and tonumber(value) or defaultValue or 0
end

function GetConfigAsBoolean(key, defaultValue)
    local value = Config.Get(key)
    return value == "true" or (defaultValue and value ~= "false")
end
```

## Configuration Usage Examples

### String Configuration
```lua
-- In metadata
configs:
  PlayerName:
    default: "Player Name"
    description: Name of the player to target

-- In code
local playerName = Config.Get("PlayerName")
```

### Integer Configuration
```lua
-- In metadata
configs:
  WaitTime:
    default: 5
    description: Time to wait in seconds

-- In code
local waitTime = tonumber(Config.Get("WaitTime"))
```

### Float Configuration
```lua
-- In metadata
configs:
  PositionX:
    default: 100.0
    description: X coordinate

-- In code
local posX = tonumber(Config.Get("PositionX"))
```

### Boolean Configuration
```lua
-- In metadata
configs:
  EnableFeature:
    default: true
    description: Enable this feature

-- In code
local enableFeature = Config.Get("EnableFeature") == "true"
```

### Choice Configuration
```lua
-- In metadata
configs:
  HubCity:
    default: "Limsa"
    description: Main city to use as hub
    is_choice: true
    choices: ["Limsa", "Gridania", "Ul'dah", "Solution Nine"]

-- In code
local hubCity = Config.Get("HubCity")
if hubCity == "Limsa" then
    -- Handle Limsa
elseif hubCity == "Gridania" then
    -- Handle Gridania
end
```

## Configuration Validation

### Validate Configuration
```lua
-- Validate configuration
function ValidateConfig(key, expectedType, required)
    local value = Config.Get(key)
    
    if required and not value then
        return false, "Required configuration missing: " .. key
    end
    
    if value and expectedType == "number" and not tonumber(value) then
        return false, "Invalid number configuration: " .. key
    end
    
    if value and expectedType == "boolean" and value ~= "true" and value ~= "false" then
        return false, "Invalid boolean configuration: " .. key
    end
    
    return true, nil
end
```

## Common Configuration Patterns

### Crafting Scripts Configuration
```lua
configs:
  CrafterClass:
    default: "Carpenter"
    description: Select the crafting class to use
    is_choice: true
    choices: ["Carpenter", "Blacksmith", "Armorer", "Goldsmith", "Leatherworker", "Weaver", "Alchemist", "Culinarian"]
  ScripColor:
    default: "Orange"
    description: Type of scrip to use (Orange, Purple)
    is_choice: true
    choices: ["Orange", "Purple"]
  HubCity:
    default: "Solution Nine"
    description: Main city to use as a hub
    is_choice: true
    choices: ["Ul'dah", "Limsa", "Gridania", "Solution Nine"]
```

### Gathering Scripts Configuration
```lua
configs:
  GatheringClass:
    default: "Miner"
    description: Select the gathering class to use
    is_choice: true
    choices: ["Miner", "Botanist", "Fisher"]
  MinInventoryFreeSlots:
    default: 5
    description: Minimum free inventory slots required
```

### Combat Scripts Configuration
```lua
configs:
  TargetName:
    default: "Enemy Name"
    description: Name of the target to attack
  UsePotion:
    default: true
    description: Use potions during combat
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Use Descriptive Names
```lua
-- Good
configs:
  MinInventorySlots:
    default: 5
    description: Minimum free inventory slots required

-- Bad
configs:
  MinSlots:
    default: 5
    description: Min slots
```

### 2. Provide Sensible Defaults
```lua
-- Good - provides reasonable default
configs:
  WaitTime:
    default: 5
    description: Time to wait in seconds

-- Bad - no default or unreasonable default
configs:
  WaitTime:
    description: Time to wait in seconds
```

### 3. Use Appropriate Types
```lua
-- Good - uses choice for limited options
configs:
  CrafterClass:
    default: "Carpenter"
    is_choice: true
    choices: ["Carpenter", "Blacksmith", "Armorer"]

-- Bad - uses string for limited options
configs:
  CrafterClass:
    default: "Carpenter"
    description: Enter crafting class name
```

### 4. Validate Configuration Values
```lua
-- Always validate critical configuration
local waitTime = tonumber(Config.Get("WaitTime"))
if not waitTime or waitTime < 0 then
    yield("/echo [Script] Invalid wait time configuration")
    StopFlag = true
end
```

